# One line ending rule for the whole repository.
#
# Text files are stored with LF in the repository, whatever the core.autocrlf
# setting of the machine that commits them happens to be. Without this rule the
# content of the repository depends on the machine, the files drift apart and
# `git add` keeps warning that LF will be replaced by CRLF. `text=auto` lets
# Git decide per file, so the binary assets below are never touched.
* text=auto

# The deployment workflow is kept exactly as it was written, byte for byte.
.github/workflows/deploy.yml -text

# Binary assets are never converted.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
